Analyze this {language} code for SOLID principle violations.

Source file:
{source}

Return a JSON array of violations. Each violation:
{{
  "principle": "S|O|L|I|D",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "violation": "description of what rule is broken",
  "suggestion": "concrete fix"
}}

S = Single Responsibility: class has more than one reason to change
O = Open/Closed: modification instead of extension pattern
L = Liskov Substitution: subclass breaks parent contract
I = Interface Segregation: fat interface, clients forced to depend on unused methods
D = Dependency Inversion: depends on concrete class instead of abstraction

Return [] if no violations found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
